{"id":"x15","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"computation","question":"Is the sum of the decimal digits of 2^79 equal to 107?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"Nothing in the question's setup rules out 107 as the digit sum.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.3,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"Digit sums of large powers of 2 can take many values, so 107 is not implausible a priori.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.3,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"2^79 equals 604462909807314587353088, a 24-digit number.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The digits of 2^79 sum to 110.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"A number's digit sum is congruent to the number mod 9.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"2^79 is congruent to 2 mod 9 because 2^6 ≡ 1 mod 9 and 79 ≡ 1 mod 6.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The digit sum 110 is congruent to 2 mod 9, consistent with the computation.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"107 is congruent to 8 mod 9, so it cannot be the digit sum of 2^79.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The mod-9 argument rules out 107 independently of the long multiplication.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":-0.9,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":-0.8,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":3,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":8,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":5,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":5,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"